BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fourth Annual World Music &amp\; Dance Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T210000
UID:691bdfe9127354636be7115d@squarespace.com
DESCRIPTION:Explore and enjoy music and dance from around the world!\nCele
 brate the rhythms\, cultures\, and global creativity that make our communi
 ty shine at the\nOccidental World Music & Dance Festival\n! This joyful\, 
 immersive event brings together extraordinary musicians and dancers from a
 round the world for a day filled with exhilarating performances\, interact
 ive workshops\, and irresistible rhythms. From captivating traditional art
 istry to innovative contemporary fusion\, the festival invites audiences o
 f all ages to experience the beauty of global cultures up close. With food
 \, vendors\, community activities\, and plenty of space to dance\, it’s 
 a feast for the senses and a celebration of unity through music and moveme
 nt. Come be part of one of Occidental’s most beloved and uplifting tradi
 tions!\nGet tickets\nTicket prices\n$75 through May 29\n$80 at the door\nK
 ids 12 and under free\, Half price for teens\nA limited number of scholars
 hips is available.\nClick here to apply for a scholarship to the event.\nM
 ore Than 50 sessions to choose from!\nEnjoy a variety of performances\, wo
 rkshops\, jams\, drum circles and demonstrations\nplus:\nMusical Instrumen
 t Lending Library\nCeltic Harp Encounter\nArt Gallery\nFree instrument che
 ck • Free parking\nLata’s Indian Cuisine\nScroll down to see the list 
 of presenters..\nOur preliminary schedule is now available! Click here to 
 view the schedule.\nSponsored by:\nLoveland Violin Shop\nLiving History Ce
 ntre\nSOLFUL\nInterested in sponsorship? Please contact us!\nKhatch Khatch
 adourian\nDodona\nPERFORMANCES\nKhatch Khatchadourian - Armenian Music\nDo
 dona - Music of Greece & Albania\nThunder Clappers Native American Dancers
 \nSol Flamenco\nJenny Kerr & Friends - Southern Delta Blues\nStory Wrens\n
 Will Marsh - Sitar music of India\nJoss Jaffe - Tabla\, West African N’g
 oni\nLos Bahianatos\nGradina - Balkan Music\nMeredith Axelrod and Craig Ve
 ntresco - Ragtime & Vintage Jazz\nCarey Dubbert and Meredith Axelrod - Aut
 oharp\nKatiana Vilá - Iberian Songs\nLos Bahianatos - Colombian Cumbia & 
 Vallenato\nMichael Hubbert - Uilleann Bagpipes\nRaman Osman - Kurdish Musi
 c\nJanessa Lynna - Belly Dance\nStory Wrens - Story Songs of the British I
 sles\nBobby Edwards - Swiss Alpenhorn\nKen Genetti - Zithers from Around t
 he World\nScroll down to see the workshops\n2026 Workshops & Demos\nClick 
 here to see workshop leaders' bios\nSlow Tunes and French Jam - Jason Adaj
 ian\nIrish Songs - Shay Black\, Hector Bragado\nIrish Fiddle - Paul Chaffe
 e\nIrish Dance - Shay Black\, Hector Bragado\, Paul Chaffee\nWake Up Your 
 Voice: A Global Singalong - Maria Culberson\nBalkan Singing - Darina Drapk
 in\nBalkan Drumming - Sean Tergis\nBalkan Dancing - Sue Williard\nBrazilia
 n Guitar - Ian Faquini\nFlamenco Dance - Joelle Goncalves\nOld Timey Jam -
  Michael Greenberg\nCuban & Puerto Rican Songs - Michael & Leslie Hubbert\
 nJazz Beyond Borders - Greg Johnson\nBlues Harmonica - Jenny Kerr\nWest Af
 rican Dance - Tyehimba Kokayi\nWest African Drumming - Lion’s Den Instit
 ute\nBelly Dance - Janessa Lynna\nCuban & Latin Drumming - Carlitos Medran
 o\nAmp Care & Repair - Philbillie Milner\nGentle Yoga - Pauline Persichili
 \nSong Circle - Celia Ramsay\nColombian Cumbia and Vallenato - Chris Reid 
 & Friends\nEasy Irish Tunes - Mark Sellin\nNative American Flute & Meditat
 ion - Al Striplen\nWomen’s Songs of Resistance - Holly Tannen\nFlamenco 
 Guitar - Mark Taylor\nRed Hot (guitar) Strings - Craig Ventresco\nIndian R
 hythms & Bols - Joss Jaffe\nArabic Drumming - Faisal Zedan\nUnlocking Your
  Voice: Friendly\nMasterclass - Sophia Zimmerman
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts\, 3850 Doris Murphy Court\, Occide
 ntal
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/world-music
 -dance-festival
X-SOURCE:Occidental Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
