DESCRIPTION:Occidental Center for the Arts presents\nMichael Capella Band\
 n\, bringing that Sonoma County-Americana sound: original songs that feel 
 instantly familiar\, blending country\, folk rock\, and blues.\nMCB brings
  a rich blend of Americana to the stage with soulful originals by award-wi
 nning songwriter Michael Capella. Their music spans country\, folk rock\, 
 and blues—-thought-provoking songs with melodies so timeless you'll swea
 r you've heard them before.\nThe band features five seasoned artists:\nMic
 hael Capella\n(vocals\, guitars)\,\nLayne Bowen\n(vocals\, guitars)\,\nLin
 da Weber\n(vocals\, percussion\, flute)\,\nKent Fossgreen\n(bass)\, and\nD
 an Ransford\n(drums\, percussion). Together\, they deliver a warm\, dynami
 c sound rooted in heartfelt storytelling and musicianship.\nTickets are $2
 5 GA\, discount for OCA members. Doors open at 2:30 PM. Bring your own sea
 t cushion or low-backed chair for our amphitheater. ADA reserved seating a
 vailable\, please contact us to request. Wine\, beer and refreshments for 
 sale. No outside food/drink allowed except water. Well-behaved dogs welcom
 e. Free parking.\nGet Ticket
